                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s, t):R \hookrightarrow A \times B
          %h3#threesorted_categorical_zfc  Three-sorted categorical ZFC
          %p
            An alternate formulation of categorical ZFC three
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sorts"} sorts
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/three-sorted+set+theory"} three-sorted set theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            between the sort of elements and the sort of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            also becomes a ternary relation between the sort of functions, and two copies of the sort of sets. There is a quinary relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} eval
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{eval}(A, B, f, a, b)
            between all three sorts, which says that given sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
